                <pb facs="0069" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg59"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/517: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Cramp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-28T17:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. The following telegram from the American Chargé d’affaires in Managua is
                    repeated for your confidential information.</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram No. 86 of August 28, 7 a.m., from the Chargé in
                    Nicaragua, printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.]</p>
                <p>Without making any inquiries whatever please telegraph your opinion in this
                    matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
